  "Security Footage: Outside Club Amour, 9 PM": "",
  "The night of the incident, 9:00 PM. We see the victim, Kume, being forced into Amour by Hamura and four Matsugane Family associates. Kume's superior, Murase, can also be seen running from the scene.": "",
  "Broken Camera": "",
  "The security camera facing Amour's rear entrance. It's broken, so there isn't any usable footage recorded on it.": "",
  "Cause of death: Puncture wound from eye to brain. Time of death: 2:00 - 3:00 AM. The murder weapon is thought to be an ice pick. There are signs of an assault and struggle while alive. The victim's blood is inconsistent with the size of the stab wound, so the body was likely moved from the real scene of the crime.": "",
  "The night of the incident, near 12 AM. Hamura strikes a Stardust host named Seiya before leaving the premises. Seiya soon witnessed Hamura enter Sauna Goten. None of Goten's guests left the building until the first train arrived the following morning. Thus, Hamura is presumed to have stayed indoors through the night.": "",
  "Cause of Death: Puncture wound from eye to brain (see: Kume's report). The murder weapon is still believed to be an ice pick. The volume of blood is once more too low, so the assault must have occurred elsewhere. The victim had neither wallet or phone, so the actual crime scene is yet unknown.": "",
  "Cause of Death: Puncture wound from eye to brain (see: Kume's report). All signs still point to an ice pick. The discrepancies between blood loss and wound size suggest another relocation of the body from the crime scene. Unfortunately, the victim had neither phone nor wallet to narrow the search.": "",
  "Shintani's Phone Log": "",
  "The numbers Shintani contacted on the day of his murder, conveniently left in his call history. Only the last call is unregistered in his address book, so that number's owner is unknown.": "",
  "A scientific study on an anti-Alzheimer's drug (AD-9) said to cure the incurable, presented in 2017 by the Advanced Drug Discovery Center. The paper was authored by the organization's leader, Prof. Ryusuke Kido. Reportedly, AD-9 passed animal testing and fully cured a lab rat of its Alzheimer's disease.": "",
  "Bullet Rifling": "",
  "Rifling mark of the bullet extracted from Shintani's corpse. It matches the pistol issued to Ayabe, an active police officer. The logical conclusion is that Shintani was shot by Ayabe's handgun.": "",
  "The audio phone data between Vice-Minister Kaoru Ichinose and Captain Hamura of the Matsugane Family.": "",
  "Waku's Hospital Room: Panorama": "",
  "The hospital room where Waku, an elderly man, stayed for two years until he was murdered. The incident details his sudden disappearance and discovery two months later, buried in the Okutama mountains.": "",
  "Cause of Death: Unknown, but suffocation seems likely. The victim, Waku, had been hospitalized for two years due to a neurcognitive disorder caused by Alzheimer's disease. When his body was found in the Okutama mountains, it was already decomposing. He most likely died soon after going missing.": "",
  "A wheeled linen hamper for patients' bed sheets at the ADDC's hospital ward. Large enough to hide a body. Multiple witnesses place a custodian named Okubo on laundry duty the day the victim escaped from his room. They distinctly remember seeing him push a laundry cart down the hall.": "",
  "Victim's Body Fluids": "",
  "Bodily fluid found in the bed of the Okubo's commercial truck by the police during the investigation after the incident. DNA tests have confirmed that the fluids belong to the victim. It turns out Okubo placed Waku in the truck bed, making it highly incriminating evidence against Okubo.": "",
  "Cause of Death: Cerebral contusion caused by over ten blows. The blood alcohol content suggests the victim was inebriated during the incident. The suspect is thought to have worn gloves while attacking, as no fingerprints were found from the victim's body. Nothing else on the crime scene has assisted police in identifying suspects.": "",
  "The blood in the scene suggests that after the victim was stabbed in the bedroom, she tried to run to the room next door while being stabbed in more than ten places. Then the gasoline was spread over the body, making the fire strongest in this area. When firefighters arrived to rescue him, Okubo was surrounded by smoke as he dashed out the entrance.": "",
  "The kitchen knife with Okubo's fingerprints on it. The victim's wounds match the shape and size of the blade.": "",
  "Security Footage: Outside Club Amour, 10 PM": "",
  "The night of the incident, 10:00 PM. Several Matsugane Family associates exit Amour, accompanied by the club's owner. Hamura is left alone in the venue with Kume, the victim. Hamura claims to have left through the back door at around midnight, but there is no evidence to support this.": "",
  "Shintani's Bullet Wounds": "",
  "Shintani was found dead inside the Yagami Detective Agency, covered in bullet wounds and hidden in a closet for an indeterminate time span. Judging by the trace amounts of blood on the floor, it is assumed that the body was moved there from the true scene of the crime.": "",
